Syntax proof on the pinned interpreter (CPython 3.14.7, `.python-version` = 3.14,
`requires-python = ">=3.14"`):

```
$ uv run python --version
Python 3.14.7
$ uv run python -c "compile('try:\n pass\nexcept ValueError, TypeError:\n pass\n','<t>','exec'); print('yes')"
BARE-EXCEPT-COMPILES: yes     # PEP 758 (Python 3.14) re-allowed bare multi-name excepts
```

Formatter behavior that forced the named-tuple resolution (ruff 0.17.3,
`target-version = "py314"` in pyproject.toml): with the reviewer's literal parenthesized
fix in the tree, `ruff format --diff` rewrites `except (A, B):` -> `except A, B:` in both
adapters, i.e. the requested spelling fails the documented `ruff format` gate; the named
tuple satisfies both the review (no bare-comma except syntax, importable on every
Python 3.x) and the gate.
